#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100992 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100687 :question/id #uuid "1b15db42-aba2-575c-a01e-b715450329fd" :question/math-academy-id "e-4379" :question/problem "Find $A+C-(B+A)$, if\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$C=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ -6 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "First, we simplify the expression by distributing the subtraction over the matrices in the parentheses: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+C-(B+A) & =A+C-B-A \\\\  & =\\cancel{A}+C-B-\\cancel{A} \\\\  & =C-B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are left with a single subtraction. So, we subtract the corresponding entries of the two matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C-B & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ -6 & 1\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3-3 & -1-(-1) \\\\ 1-2 & 2-0 \\\\ -6-(-4) & 1-1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "16e62b0e-adda-5d35-aeb9-961057dce8f0" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049939 :topic/id #uuid "20058901-3844-51ce-a107-70205a1553fb" :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054686} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054760} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054765}] :topic/math-academy-id 137 :topic/next [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048267} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048511} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048524} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048764} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048863} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049496} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049846} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050099} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050661} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051079}] :topic/title "Distributing the Negative Sign in a Linear Expression"}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17